      "hints": [
        "Integrate: $[\\frac{2}{3}x^{3/2} + 4x^{1/2}]_1^4$.",
        "Evaluate: $(\\frac{16}{3} + 8) - (\\frac{2}{3} + 4) = \\frac{40}{3} - \\frac{14}{3} = \\frac{26}{3}$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Express the integrand in index form and integrate:\n$$\\int_1^4 \\left( x^{1/2} + 2x^{-1/2} \\right)\\,dx = \\left[ \\frac{x^{3/2}}{\\frac{3}{2}} + \\frac{2x^{1/2}}{\\frac{1}{2}} \\right]_1^4 = \\left[ \\frac{2}{3}x^{3/2} + 4x^{1/2} \\right]_1^4$$",
        "Substitute the limits $x = 4$ and $x = 1$:\n$$\\text{At } x = 4: \\quad \\frac{2}{3}(4^{3/2}) + 4(4^{1/2}) = \\frac{2}{3}(8) + 4(2) = \\frac{16}{3} + 8 = \\frac{40}{3}$$\n$$\\text{At } x = 1: \\quad \\frac{2}{3}(1^{3/2}) + 4(1^{1/2}) = \\frac{2}{3} + 4 = \\frac{14}{3}$$",
        "Subtract the lower limit value from the upper limit value:\n$$\\frac{40}{3} - \\frac{14}{3} = \\frac{26}{3} \\quad \\left(\\text{or } 8\\frac{2}{3} \\approx 8.67\\right)$$"
      ],
      "checking": {
